<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Muhammadiyah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Muhammadiyah is an Indonesian Islamic organisation founded in Yogyakarta in 1912 by Ahmad Dahlan. A modernist movement, it called for a return to the Qur'an and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadith">hadith</a>, criticised practices it saw as unorthodox and promoted modern education. It runs thousands of schools, universities, hospitals and clinics and is, after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahdlatul-ulama">Nahdlatul Ulama</a>, the second largest Muslim mass organisation in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, with tens of millions of followers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/muhammadiyah.jpg" alt="Muhammadiyah" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: K. H. Siradj Dahlan. Vector by Hibensis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Muhammadiyah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
